  "answer": "<p><b>AWS Cost Explorer</b> is a dedicated tool that allows you to track, analyze, and visualize your historical and forecasted AWS spending, which is essential for cost monitoring. Setting up <b>budgets in the billing section</b> lets you define spending thresholds and receive alerts when your usage nears or exceeds your budget, providing proactive control over finances. <b>Trusted Advisor</b> offers personalized recommendations, including those for cost optimization, helping you to identify resources that can be adjusted or terminated to cut costs.<br><br><i>Aggregating logs in CloudWatch Logs and manually inspecting them for billing data</i> is not practical nor intended for cost tracking or optimization; AWS provides specialized tools like Cost Explorer and billing dashboards for these purposes. Both <i>AWS Budgets</i> and <i>Trusted Advisor</i> offer specific insights and notifications aimed at managing and optimizing costs efficiently, while <i>Cost Explorer</i> enables detailed analysis of usage patterns for better financial visibility.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Always configure AWS Budgets and set up Cost Explorer early in the project lifecycle. Periodically review Trusted Advisor recommendations to identify saving opportunities. Avoid relying on CloudWatch Logs for any kind of financial monitoring, as it is designed for resource operational insights, not billing.</p>",
  "query": "<p>Your organization makes use of a variety of AWS resources, and the IT lead is worried about rising cloud expenses. What methods can be leveraged to monitor and control AWS costs as well as identify cost-saving opportunities?<br>Choose <b>three</b> answers from the options listed below.</p>",
